**Boundary 16.1 (historical images are not whole service domains).** A
recognizes exactly its known-unit, nonnegative-endpoint, positive-internal-
gap raw-clock image. It does not recover arbitrary zero-gap histories,
unknown seeds, Reset-closed journals or arbitrary Add interventions.
C recovers pure clocked words with its known origin and changed digital
Read. It does not recover literal nuisance journals or arbitrary
bounded-error observations. Current exact/set-valued service in §7 is
broader in each installation and survives leaving those historical
images. Membership, provenance, access, recoverability and current
callability are distinct assertions with the separate premises stated
above.

